# CODEOWNERS — GitHub requests these reviewers automatically on a PR and,
# combined with a branch protection rule ("require review from Code Owners"),
# BLOCKS merging until the right person approves.
#
# Demo point: change a file below in a branch, open a PR, and watch GitHub
# auto-assign the reviewer. This is how a data team stops someone from
# merging a schema or infra change without the DBA / platform owner seeing it.
#
# Syntax:  <path pattern>   <@owner> [@owner2 ...]
# Replace the placeholder handles with real GitHub usernames/teams before use.

# Everything, by default
*                       @the-surfing-dba

# Database change owners
/sqlserver/             @the-surfing-dba
/mysql/                 @the-surfing-dba
/mongo/                 @the-surfing-dba

# Infrastructure needs an extra set of eyes — highest blast radius
/terraform/             @the-surfing-dba

# CI/CD and repo policy changes
/.github/               @the-surfing-dba
